I upgraded a DS10L from RH 6.2 to 7.2.  the system is just fine until 
the disk is accessed, and then it hangs there for about 60 seconds 
before continuing on as if nothing has happened.  the disk activity LED 
is on when this happens.  for example, i can sit there at a shell 
prompt, do a "man ls", and then the system will freeze up for a minute. 
  the load average jumps to over 3.  i didn't notice this under RH 6.2, 
and i don't notice it on another DS10L i upgraded to 7.2.  it could 
have been present under 6.2 without me know it since this system wasn't 
in use when i upgraded it.

any ideas?

---Matt




